  In a #bowl{}, mix the @precooked corn flour{2%cups} with @water{2%cups} and @salt{1%pinch}, until a soft and manageable dough is obtained.

> The amount of water may vary according to the brand of flour, but generally a ratio of 1:1 (one part flour to one part water) is used.

Form balls of dough approximately 2-3 inches in diameter and flatten them to form the arepas. Make sure they are evenly thick so they cook evenly.

Preheat the #Air Fryer{} to 400 degrees Fahrenheit (approximately 200 degrees Celsius) for about ~{5%minutes}.

Place the arepas in the #Air Fryer basket{} and cook for about ~{10-15%minutes}, turning them halfway through the cooking time so that they cook evenly.

Once the arepas are golden brown and crispy on the outside and soft on the inside, remove them from the Air Fryer and let them cool for a few minutes before serving.